meta {
  name: Poll ingest progress
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/ingest-progress/{{progressToken}}
}

docs {
  Real chunk-embedding progress for an in-flight ad-hoc ingest — poll this in parallel with
  a `Learn an attachment into memory` request that was sent with the same `progress_token`
  query param. Embedding a large document (e.g. a whole zip's concatenated text) can take
  minutes on a CPU-only machine, and this is what a UI polls instead of showing nothing.

  204 (empty body) if the token is unknown: never started, already finished and aged out
  (5 minutes), or nobody will ever start it. Not an error — the caller is racing this
  against the POST that owns the token, so "nothing yet" is a normal answer.

  200 body: `{"done": <chunks embedded>, "total": <chunks total>}`. `total` of 0 means
  extraction/chunking hasn't finished yet — the count itself isn't known.
}
